    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d628">

                <pb facs="0918" n="782" xml:id="pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3356: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Moore</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-27T20:00:00-05:00">April 27, 1929—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>86. I assume that my telegram number 84<anchor n="29" xml:id="d628-f1"/> which
                    probably reached you after you had sent your 49<anchor n="29" xml:id="d628-f2"/>
                    to me answers this telegram and also your 48.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d628-f3"/>
                    Am I correct?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
